body:
FEATURE SPEC: Autosave restore visual indicator

Priority: Medium
ADHD rationale: Kai refreshes mid-exam. Answers silently reappear. He might not notice
and could think the test restarted. ADHD users benefit from explicit state confirmation.

CURRENT BEHAVIOR
exam.html lines 370-373: restoreAutosave() runs after loadExam(), then input listener starts.
If Kai had answered 8/15 questions, refreshes, and reopens -- all 8 answers silently reappear.
No message. No animation. Just populated inputs.

PROPOSED BEHAVIOR
After restoreAutosave(), if ANY inputs were restored:
  1. Show a brief inline toast or status bar at the top of questionsContainer
  2. Content: "8 answers restored. Keep going. 💾"
  3. Auto-dismiss after 3 seconds (or on first input event)
  4. Must NOT be an alert() -- see Section 16 of .design-system.md

IMPLEMENTATION SPEC

In exam.html restoreAutosave() function (line 209):
  Count the number of non-empty inputs restored.
  If count > 0, call: showRestoreToast(count);

function showRestoreToast(count) {
  var el = document.createElement('div');
  el.id = 'restore-toast';
  el.setAttribute('role', 'status');
  el.setAttribute('aria-live', 'polite');
  el.style.cssText = [
    'background:var(--bg-highlight)',
    'border:1px solid var(--border-default)',
    'border-radius:8px',
    'padding:10px 16px',
    'margin-bottom:12px',
    'font-size:var(--text-sm)',
    'color:var(--text-secondary)',
    'text-align:center'
  ].join(';');
  el.textContent = count + ' answer' + (count > 1 ? 's' : '') + ' restored. Keep going. 💾';
  var container = document.getElementById('questionsContainer');
  if (container && container.firstChild) {
    container.insertBefore(el, container.firstChild);
  }
  // Auto-dismiss
  setTimeout(function() { if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el); }, 3000);
  // Dismiss on first input
  container.addEventListener('input', function onInput() {
    if (el.parentNode) el.parentNode.removeChild(el);
    container.removeEventListener('input', onInput);
  }, { once: true });
}

REDUCED MOTION
No animation needed. Toast appears instantly, disappears after 3s.
prefers-reduced-motion: N/A (no transition or animation used).

EDGE CASES
- If 0 inputs restored: no toast (user sees fresh state)
- If restoreAutosave() fails (parse error): no toast (catch block)
- sessionStorage cleared after gradeExam() (line 1055): no restore on post-grade refresh

NOTE ON SCOPE
This is sessionStorage only (same tab, refresh). If Kai closes browser and reopens,
sessionStorage is gone -- no restore, no toast. Correct behavior -- exam is meant to
complete in one sitting. This spec does NOT change that behavior.
